<qti-assessment-item xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0 https://purl.imsglobal.org/spec/qti/v3p0/schema/xsd/imsqti_asiv3p0_v1p0.xsd" identifier="pcb-item-82a3eec4dd784cb193f7bcec5bfba114" title="sat-c2-u18-utilitarian.html qc1" adaptive="true" time-dependent="false">
  <qti-response-declaration identifier="RESPONSE" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-correct-response><qti-value>A</qti-value></qti-correct-response>
  </qti-response-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="SCORE" cardinality="single" base-type="float"><qti-default-value><qti-value>0</qti-value></qti-default-value></qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="FEEDBACK" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier"/>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-default-value><qti-value>show_interaction</qti-value></qti-default-value>
  </qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-item-body>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="show_interaction" outcome-identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" show-hide="show" class="qti-margin-0">
      <qti-content-body>
        <p>Which sentence uses &quot;utilitarian&quot; correctly?</p>
    <qti-choice-interaction response-identifier="RESPONSE" shuffle="true" max-choices="1">
      <qti-simple-choice identifier="A">The clinic chose utilitarian flooring — seamless gray sheets that shrug off bleach and gurney wheels — over the patterned tile the donors had preferred.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="B">Shoppers adored the boutique&apos;s utilitarian window display, a swirl of silk ribbons and fairy lights arranged purely to delight the passing eye.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="C">Held together with tape and missing half its keys, the lounge&apos;s utilitarian piano could no longer manage even a full scale.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="D">The gala&apos;s utilitarian gowns, sewn from hand-beaded lace, each demanded three fittings and could not survive a light rain.</qti-simple-choice>
    </qti-choice-interaction>
      </qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>

    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-A" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Correct! Utilitarian means designed strictly for usefulness, so it&apos;s the correct answer because the flooring was chosen for what it withstands — bleach and gurney wheels — with the prettier tile passed over entirely.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-B" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Utilitarian means designed strictly for usefulness, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because ribbons and fairy lights arranged &apos;purely to delight the eye&apos; are decoration doing no work — the reverse of use-first design.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-C" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Utilitarian means designed strictly for usefulness, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because a taped-up piano that cannot manage a scale no longer serves any use at all — broken is not the same as built for work.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-D" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Utilitarian means designed strictly for usefulness, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because hand-beaded lace needing three fittings and shelter from rain puts beauty ahead of function at every turn.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
  </qti-item-body>
  <qti-response-processing>
